WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:05.100
The families who live here are among the poorest
in Rio de la Plata.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:20.649
There's not even running water in the wooden
huts they built themselves.

00:00:20.649 --> 00:00:25.590
This woman is explaining to Nicolas Wertheimer
that she gets water from a pump and a hose

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.040
that extends through the reeds.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:36.100
The water comes from the Rio de la Plata - but
it's polluted, and poses a health risk.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:42.970
Nicolas Wertheimer wants to improve the situation
and founded the project 'Agua Segura' to ensure

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.420
the local water supply is clean and safe.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.180
Local children are often sick from drinking
contaminated water.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.220
Their mothers have no one to turn to for help.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.120
“Is diarrhea also a problem?”

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.700
“Yes, it is...My little one was throwing up, and
was taken to hospital.”

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.780
“Did he get antibiotics?”

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.580
“No, they didn't give him anything.”

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.200
To tackle the problem, Nikolas Wertheimer
is installing a water filter that doesn't

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.700
need electricity.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.240
"This is a filter.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:35.299
Families who drink water from the river can
position it on a wall, fill it up, and the

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.180
clean water comes out here.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:43.660
It needs to collect in a container that's
clean and not contaminated."

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.200
"My whole life long, I've dreamt of changing
the world.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.260
I worked in a 
hospital as a surgeon and internist, but I

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:01.369
didn't feel I was doing what I'd always dreamt
of.

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:07.380
One day I googled: 'what do you need to change the world', and I came across this clean water technology.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:13.310
I thought of all the people made sick by contaminated
water, so I made some calls with a view to

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:14.580
introducing it here."

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.560
Wertheimer also managed to persuade
the well-known Argentinian TV presenter

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.160
Julian Weich to support the project.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.080
"There's a major problem with clean drinking
water in Argentina - and indeed across the world.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.019
Nicolas is addressing the issue not just
because he's a doctor but because he wants

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:36.079
to solve a problem, I trust him.

00:02:36.079 --> 00:02:37.079
I believe in him.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.240
We're supporting each other in a bid to find
a solution."

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.019
A few hundred families live along this part
of the river.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.500
It can only be reached by water.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.060
Wertheimer spends a lot of time on
the phone sorting things out.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.040
Today he's accompanying some local children
to school.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:58.560
Julian und Nicolas founded the Agua
Segura initiative in late 2015.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.100
They see themselves as social entrepeneuers.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:10.080
Children's health is one of their first priorities.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.560
Their digestive systems are more vulnerable
than adults' - they have lower immunity to

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.920
parasites in contaminated water.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:26.340
At school, the children get breakfast and
lunch - and now, clean water too.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.720
"I'm very pleased.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.400
The principal is very committed and always
gives us a warm welcome."

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.640
"The device works by itself.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.809
It doesn't need an electricity supply, and
you don't don't need to add chemicals.

00:03:40.809 --> 00:03:45.129
The operating principle is the weight of the
water - it flows through pores that are 20

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:50.049
nanometers in diameter, so bacteria, viruses
and parasites are filtered out.

00:03:50.049 --> 00:03:51.960
This is clean, safe drinking water."

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.060
The filter costs several hundred dollars and
lasts 5 years.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:04.300
It's financed by donations - and increasingly,
with public money too.

00:04:08.709 --> 00:04:12.640
These kids are also taught about water in the
classroom.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.749
They take the lessons they've learnt home
with them.

00:04:15.749 --> 00:04:20.730
Slowly but surely, the health issues related
to contiminated drinking water are beginning

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.730
to subside in Rio de la Plata.

